// Rule: [T1574.001] Quickfox - Fdmtp Csmonitor DLL Sideloading
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1574.001
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceImageLoadEvents
// Purpose: Campaign hunt for csmonitor.exe loading a co-located Microsoft.ServiceHosting.T ools.dll from the source-observed QuickFox staging directory.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceImageLoadEvents for fdmtp csmonitor dll sideloading using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: The endpoint recorded the source-observed loader, module and staging-directory relationship and requires immediate file validation.
// A match does not prove: FDMTP execution or attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// QuickFox / FDMTP - csmonitor.exe DLL sideloading
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceImageLoadEvents
//
// Source evidence: FortiGuard IR observed csmonitor.exe loading a malicious
// Microsoft.ServiceHosting.Tools.dll from the same
// ...\quickfox\updated directory in both loader generations.
//
// A match does not prove FDMTP execution or attribution. Validate the loader
// and DLL hashes, signatures, file origin, software ownership, and follow-on
// process/network activity before disposition.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "csmonitor.exe"
| where FileName =~ "Microsoft.ServiceHosting.Tools.dll"
| where FolderPath =~ InitiatingProcessFolderPath
| where FolderPath endswith @"\quickfox\updated"
| project Timestamp,
          DeviceId,
          DeviceName,
          InitiatingProcessAccountName,
          InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessSHA1,
          FolderPath,
          FileName,
          SHA1,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
